      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I understand the test. The original has several understandability issues:\n1. The `data_samples()` method provides `{PaxDate, LocalDate}` pairs, but `iso` (the `LocalDate`) is never used in the test body.\n2. Many unused data provider methods clutter the file.\n3. All data is crammed onto single lines.\n4. Several unused imports.\n\nI'll write an improved version with a dedicated, well-formatted data provider that only returns `PaxDate` instances, and remove all unused code.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version improves understandability by removing the unused `LocalDate iso` parameter and its corresponding data provider pairs, eliminating the 10+ unused data provider methods, formatting the test data with one entry per line and grouped by semantic category (epoch, leap years, century boundaries, BCE dates), and reducing imports to only the two actually needed."
